<title>JAPAN: Konica to sell diagnostic drug for cancer.</title>
<headline>Konica to sell diagnostic drug for cancer.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese camera and film maker Konica Corp said on Wednesday that it would start marketing a diagnostic drug for ovary cancer on July 22.</p>
<p>The drug, GAT-EIA, detects cancer by measuring the amount of galactosyltransferase associated with tumor (GAT) in the blood, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>A single kit, which can conduct 100 tests, will be priced at 100,000 yen, it said.</p>
<p>A Konica spokesman said that the company does not have any target figure for sales.</p>
</text>
